<!-- UseEffectiveCount :Determines whether rate limits are tracked locally per Message Processor
(false) or synchronized globally across the region (true)   -->

<!-- <Identifier>  : Specifies the custom variable (such as client IP, developer ID, or API key) used
to uniquely track and isolate rate-limiting counts per client. -->

<!-- <MessageWeight>  : Dynamically assigns a heavier transaction cost to specific requests (e.g.,
resource-intensive queries counting as 5 requests instead of 1).-->

<!-- <Rate>  : Defines the maximum allowed frequency of incoming requests (e.g., 50ps for 50 requests
per second or 10pm for 10 per minute). -->